==============================================================================
APPLICATION INFORMATION
KAZE Traders Business Manager
==============================================================================

Name
    KAZE Traders Business Manager (also called Kaze)

What it is
    A web application for small traders and small businesses. It helps you
    record stock, sales, customers, suppliers, cash, bookkeeping documents,
    journals, and simple financial statements from a browser.

Who it is for
    Owners and staff of a small shop or trading business. Accounts can be
    created as "owner" or "staff". The owner can add team members, change
    settings, export or clear business data, and open every module.

What it is not
    This is a practical day-to-day record keeper. It is not a replacement
    for a qualified accountant, auditor, lawyer, or tax office. Figures
    such as profit and loss, tax summaries, and balance sheets are tools
    to help you see your own numbers. Always check official rules in your
    country before you file tax or legal papers.

Main modules
    - Dashboard          overview, goals, charts, activity
    - Stock              inventory, SKU, low-stock alerts, valuation
    - Sales              invoices from stock, discounts, aged sales
    - Customers          contacts, statements
    - Suppliers          supplier list
    - Purchase orders    buying from suppliers
    - Book keeping       quotations, invoices, receipts, notes, payroll
                         slips, bank slips, and related source documents
    - Account tracking   cash book, journals, ledgers, trading account,
                         profit and loss, balance sheet, cash flow
    - Budgets            planned vs actual
    - Recurring items    repeating income or costs
    - Reports            filtered summaries and charts
    - Documents          printable business papers
    - SWOT / Plan        simple strategy notes
    - Tasks / Notes      work list and memos
    - Calendar           dated items
    - Reminders          due dates in one place
    - Tax                simple tax / VAT style summary
    - Calculator         quick profit maths
    - Team               staff accounts (owner)
    - Settings           business name, currency, theme, backup, clear data
    - Notifications      in-app alerts
    - Search             find records across modules

Technical notes
    Runtime:        Python 3.11 (see runtime.txt)
    Framework:      Flask
    Login:          Flask-Login and Werkzeug password hashing
    Database:       PostgreSQL through psycopg2 (DATABASE_URL)
    PDFs:           ReportLab
    Charts:         Chart.js (loaded in the browser)
    Icons:          Lucide
    Process:        Gunicorn for production
    Dependencies:   listed in requirements.txt

    Flask
    Flask-Login
    Werkzeug
    gunicorn
    psycopg2-binary
    reportlab

Data and privacy
    Business records belong to the signed-in business (owner id). Staff
    see the same business data. Passwords are stored hashed, not in plain
    text. A backup export and an owner-only "clear data" reset are
    available in Settings. Clearing data removes business records so you
    can start again; it does not delete the owner login itself.

